From 36122f4c2264e868f3df36a1cac0bc41caf2fee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:58:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] Agent notifications and unread dots for CLI agents in
 embedded builds

The remote PTY's init line now sets what desktop's PTY environment does for CLI agent
plugins (TERM_PROGRAM, WARP_CLIENT_VERSION, WARP_CLI_AGENT_PROTOCOL_VERSION), so Warp's
Claude Code plugin sends structured status events: agents in panel tabs get the done /
needs-input notifications and the unread dot in the vertical tabs, like desktop. The
Agents panel shows the same dot on a conversation that runs in a Warp pane, and clicking
it goes to that pane.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
